1
00:00:05,876 --> 00:00:12,062
Goals, metrics and check-ins. Create a goal, measure it, record progress

2
00:00:12,611 --> 00:00:16,452
To create a goal, click New goal in the Goals header.

3
00:00:16,588 --> 00:00:21,451
Write the title as an outcome. It's the only required field.

4
00:00:21,554 --> 00:00:25,523
A target date lets GoalNexa predict whether you'll make it.

5
00:00:25,623 --> 00:00:26,945
Click Create.

6
00:00:28,864 --> 00:00:34,063
Now measure it. Click the plus on the goal's row, and choose Add metric.

7
00:00:34,157 --> 00:00:38,462
A metric is one number. Give it a name and a unit.

8
00:00:38,567 --> 00:00:46,716
The base value is where you start. The target is where you want to be. Here it's lower, because faster is better.

9
00:00:46,846 --> 00:00:53,160
Each check-in is a new reading here. For things like kilometres run, choose an amount to add instead.

10
00:00:56,493 --> 00:01:02,250
Now record progress. On the metric's plus, choose Check in.

11
00:01:02,374 --> 00:01:08,688
Enter the value. Leave When blank for now, or set it to backdate. Add a note if you like.

12
00:01:08,784 --> 00:01:14,494
Click Save check-in. The chart, progress and health update right away.

13
00:01:14,648 --> 00:01:20,277
To edit or delete, click the goal's name. The side panel has Edit and Delete.

14
00:01:20,444 --> 00:01:23,681
This was just a demo, so let's delete it.
